    "stickyHide": {
      "page": "player",
      "text": "Hide text = Blur practice (H), drawn as word shapes instead of a blur.\n\nSame rule as today: the playing line never reveals itself. Hover (desktop) or press-and-hold (touch) peeks one line. Translation and IPA stay hidden with it.\n\nWord shapes are flat fills — no per-line blur layer to paint.",
      "w": 380,
      "x": 5520,
      "y": 1320
    },
    "stickyLogo": {
      "page": "system",
      "text": "Logo alignment\n\n• Original = logo blue #4797F5. You = logo violet, deepened to #8B2FE0 for contrast. Brand = the logo gradient, deepened for white labels.\n• Blue and violet are close in hue, so the original is always the translucent layer and you the solid one (pitch, buttons, loop).\n• Echo lens fades through the logo’s opacity steps 1 / 0.65 / 0.35.",
      "w": 380,
      "x": 2320,
      "y": 0
    },
    "stickyParity": {
      "page": "player",
      "text": "Nothing here is a new feature.\n\n• Listen = today's player. Echo = echo mode: the loop pauses and rewinds at its end — it never auto-loops.\n• Loop handles = [ ] { } (expand / shrink echo).\n• Original = replay (S). Record = R. A take plays from its chip (G plays the selected one). Score = assessment (V). Share = practice poster, top bar, in Echo once there are takes. Pitch = pitch contour (P).\n• Notes on words come from the stored Azure assessment (error type + per-word accuracy + phonemes).\n• The margin replaces the lookup dialog and the assessment dialog on wide windows.",
      "w": 380,
      "x": 6080,
      "y": 0
    },
    "stickyPhone": {
      "page": "phone",
      "text": "Phones stay portrait (ADR-0059).\n\nThe margin becomes a bottom sheet. The mode switch sits at the top on every size, because it changes how the whole page reads; every action lives in the dock under the thumb.",
      "w": 340,
      "x": 2820,
      "y": 0
    }
  },
